VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Rampwise//Event plan//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:Sprint triathlon plan
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-23-swim1-swim-technique-and-a@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261123T063000
DTEND:20261123T065500
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: technique and aerobic (25 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim + kick\; 10 min drills (catch-up\, fingertip d
 rag\, sculling)\; 10 min steady aerobic\, RPE 3\; 5 min cool-down. Swim t
 ime and effort\, not distance: pools and paces differ. If you know your 1
 00 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 15-30 s between repeats.\
 n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move mea
 ns stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-run1-easy-run-with-stride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261124T063000
DTEND:20261124T070500
SUMMARY:[RW] Easy run with strides (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 12 min easy\; 6 x (0.33 min hard + 1 min easy
 )\; 5 min cool-down. Six relaxed fast strides of about 20 s (RPE 7\, smoo
 th\, not a sprint) with easy jogging between. Easy means RPE 2-3: you can
  talk in full sentences. Use your watch's easy heart-rate zone if you hav
 e one.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you m
 ove means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-24-str1-strength-lower-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261124T183000
DTEND:20261124T190500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: lower body (squat and hinge) (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:Triathlon (long distance): better cycling and running economy 
 across a 26-week block. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a set if for
 m breaks. Strength starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice).\n\nWe
 ek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means st
 op.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-bike1-ride-with-cadence-dr@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261125T063000
DTEND:20261125T071500
SUMMARY:[RW] Ride with cadence drills (45 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 9 min easy\; 6 x (0.5 min steady + 2.5 min ea
 sy)\; 8 min cool-down. Six short high-cadence spins (about 100 rpm\, smoo
 th)\, easy between. Skill\, not strength. Do not do this right before a r
 un: high cadence raises the cost of the run that follows (Walsh 2019).\n\
 nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means
  stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-26-swim2-swim-aerobic-enduran@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261126T063000
DTEND:20261126T065500
SUMMARY:[RW] Swim: aerobic endurance (25 min)
DESCRIPTION:8 min easy swim\; 10 min steady aerobic with a few 25 m kicks\
 ; 5 min cool-down. Swim time and effort\, not distance: pools and paces d
 iffer. If you know your 100 m time\, convert the minutes to metres. Rest 
 15-30 s between repeats.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that
  changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-26-str2-strength-upper-body-@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261126T183000
DTEND:20261126T190500
SUMMARY:[RW] Strength: upper body and trunk (pull and push) (35 min)
DESCRIPTION:Triathlon (long distance): better cycling and running economy 
 across a 26-week block. Lift with 2-3 reps in reserve\, stop a set if for
 m breaks. Strength starts at least 3 hours after cardio (practice).\n\nWe
 ek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means st
 op.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-28-bike_long-long-ride@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20261128T063000
DTEND:20261128T072500
SUMMARY:[RW] Long ride (55 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 35 min easy\; 10 min cool-down. Mostly steady
  endurance (RPE 2-3\, 56-75 % of FTP if you use power). Eat and drink on 
 rides over 90 minutes.\n\nWeek 1 (BASE). Not medical advice\; pain that c
 hanges how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
